-- [TABLET NODE: P3511T1CyclicDissection]

/-!
# P3511T1CyclicDissection

Adapted from Wesley Pegden’s Apache-2.0 Trellis formalization of Levine–Pegden–Smart.
Changes: pool module paths, public exports, project namespace and current Mathlib compatibility.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace ApollonianSuperharmonic

/--
For an index type $A$, a cyclic dissection relates a boundary list $L$
to a list of ordered triples $F$.  It is generated by the following
three rules, and no others.  The list $[a,b,c]$ has the single face
$(a,b,c)$.  If $U,V$ are nonempty lists, a dissection of
$[a]+U+[b]$ with faces $F_1$ and a dissection of $[b]+V+[a]$
with faces $F_2$ give a dissection of $[a]+U+[b]+V$ with faces
$F_1+F_2$.  Finally a dissection of a cyclic rotation of $L$ gives a
dissection of $L$ with the same ordered face list.
Here $+$ denotes list concatenation.  Distinctness of the boundary
indices is imposed by applications, not by this inductive relation.
The split rule saves the two complementary cyclic arcs, their common
endpoint pair, and both smaller dissections.  Thus it records
noninterleaving diagonal recursion, not merely a list of faces or an
edge-incidence count.  It contains no coordinates or separation claim.
-/
inductive P3511T1CyclicDissection (α : Type) :
    List α → List (Fin 3 → α) → Prop where
-- BODY
  | triangle (a b c : α) :
      P3511T1CyclicDissection α [a, b, c] [![a, b, c]]
  | split (a b : α) (u v : List α) (left right : List (Fin 3 → α))
      (hu : 0 < u.length) (hv : 0 < v.length)
      (hleft : P3511T1CyclicDissection α (a :: (u ++ [b])) left)
      (hright : P3511T1CyclicDissection α (b :: (v ++ [a])) right) :
      P3511T1CyclicDissection α (a :: (u ++ b :: v)) (left ++ right)
  | rotate (boundary : List α) (faces : List (Fin 3 → α)) (k : Nat)
      (h : P3511T1CyclicDissection α (boundary.rotate k) faces) :
      P3511T1CyclicDissection α boundary faces

end ApollonianSuperharmonic

end
